    "id": "v2-ee1e0-p32-practice-slot-13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Mia and Noah are two of the students standing in a row. Find the number of ways the students can be arranged so that at least two students stand between Mia and Noah, if the row has:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "v2-ee1e0-p32-practice-slot-13-slot-13-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "7 students",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2400$",
          "worked": "Total arrangements: $7!=5040$.\n\nNo student between: treat MN as one unit.\n$$6!\\times2!=1440$$\nOne student between: choose the student, then treat M?N as one unit.\n$$5\\times5!\\times2!=1200$$\nThese cases do not overlap.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\text{Acceptable arrangements}&=5040-1440-1200\\\\&=2400\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 45
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-ee1e0-p32-practice-slot-13-slot-13-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "8 students",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$21\\,600$",
          "worked": "Total arrangements: $8!=40\\,320$.\n\nNo student between: treat MN as one unit.\n$$7!\\times2!=10\\,080$$\nOne student between: choose the student, then treat M?N as one unit.\n$$6\\times6!\\times2!=8640$$\nThese cases do not overlap.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\text{Acceptable arrangements}&=40\\,320-10\\,080-8640\\\\&=21\\,600\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 45
      }
    ]
